istering, please do the following on Sept. 30th :**\n\n1. **✅ Do your best to arrive on time @ Café Princess (6:30 PM)**\n1. **✅ Tell us whether you want to focus on learning/practicing ENGLISH or KOREAN**\n1. **✅ Tell us your level: Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced or Expert**\n1. **✅** **Buy 1 item from the Café Princess Menu** **(This is the only cost if this is your 1st or 2nd class. There is an additional $5 fee starting from your third class onwards)**\n\n**\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-**\n**✨ Popular menu items include:**\n\n* ***🍓 Strawberry Cheesecake Bingsu***\n* ***🍧 Mango or Oreo Bingsu***\n* ***☕ Matcha \u0026 Tiramisu Lattes***\n* ***🧇 Princess Waffles with Ice Cream \u0026 Much More***\n\n**###** **What to Expect**\n\n* ***🇰🇷 Guided Korean \u0026 English language practice***\n* ***📚 Interactive mini-lesson led by an award-winning certified teacher***\n* ***🗣️ Structured conversation activities with native and fluent speakers***\n* ***🎲 Board games and social activities to practice language naturally***\n* ***🤝 Make new friends while improving your communication skills***\n\n**👨‍🏫** **MEET YOUR TEACHER \u0026 HOST**\n**###** **Learn From an Expert Language Teacher**\n\n***John Dias (OCT, PhD researcher, MA, BEd, HBA \u0026 EELC) is an award-winning certified language teacher with 10+ years experience***\n\n**###** **Who Should Attend?**\n\n* ***English learners (ESL)***\n* ***Native Korean speakers wanting to practice English***\n* ***Korean learners of all levels***\n* ***International students, newcomers, professionals, and anyone interested in language and culture***\n\n**Feel free to** **📧** **e-mail [info@tilelearning.com](mailto:info@tilelearning.com) if you have any questions.**\n**Check out our** **🌐** **[website](https://www.tilelearning.com/) and [instagram](https://www.instagram.com/tilelearning/) accounts for more details.**","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetu